[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127937,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Verrucous venous malformation is a distinctive localized vascular malformation associated with overlying prominent epidermal changes.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127938,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9142/0 Verrucous venous malformation</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127939,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F2Y &amp; XH23S6 Other specified benign cutaneous neoplasms &amp; Verrucous keratotic haemangioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127940,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> verrucous haemangioma (obsolete); verrucous venulocapillary malformation; verrucous keratotic haemangioma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127941,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127942,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These lesions have a predilection for the distal extremities; occasionally they occur on the trunk.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127943,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesions are slightly raised singular, grouped, or confluent red to purple plaques that become more hyperkeratotic and may ulcerate, bleed, and slowly enlarge over time. Linear lesions have been reported {10688730}. Local tissue hypertrophy is not a feature.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127944,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is a rare congenital lesion with no sex predilection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127945,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not known</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127946,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Verrucous venous malformation is non-familial. A somatic missense mutation in <em>MAP3K3</em> has been identified in some cases {25728774}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127947,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127948,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>An epidermis with prominent acanthosis, papillomatosis, hyperkeratosis, parakeratosis, and crusting overlies an expanded papillary dermis with numerous dilated and congested capillaries and venules, often extending into the investing dermis of the skin adnexa while sparing the reticular dermis. The subcutaneous tissue displays an increased density of variably congested capillaries and venules, with occasionally admixed larger veins. Mitotic activity is rare to absent. There may be focal light endothelial positivity for GLUT1, but the full placenta-like vascular phenotype of infantile haemangioma is lacking. Small dilated lymphatic vessels also may be present but the predominant differentiation is clearly blood vascular {10886755; 6038751; 25263605}.</p>\r\n<h6>Differential diagnosis</h6>\r\n<p>The superficial dermal changes closely resemble angiokeratoma. Histological distinction relies on the identification of a deep dermal&nbsp;/ subcutaneous component.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127949,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
